### erreur500, + a structured JSON log on the server side (docker compose logs backend)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles

### ==========================================================
### DAY 17: basic security (helmet, rate limiting, protection
### of the GET /:id/reviews route).
###
### Helmet + global rate limiting cannot be tested with a single
### request: check the security headers on any
### response above (Content-Security-Policy, X-Frame-Options,
### Strict-Transport-Security...). To really trigger a 429,
### loop requests from a terminal:
###   for i in $(seq 1 12); do curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" \
###     -X POST http://localhost:4000/api/auth/login \
###     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
###     -d '{"email":"nobody@test.com","password":"wrongpass"}'; done
### -> the first 10: 401, from the 11th on: 429.
### The auth limiter ignores successful attempts (skipSuccessfulRequests),
### so the same loop with a correct password keeps returning 200.
### ==========================================================

