### ==========================================================
### DAY 18: Public API module - authentication with an API key
### (in addition to the session cookie), documented in API.md.
### ==========================================================

### Create an account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "apikey18@example.com",
  "name": "ApiKey18",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Generate an API key (with the current session cookie)
# @name createApiKeyDay18
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/api-keys

### Log out (no valid cookie from here on)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

### Use the API key for /me, WITHOUT a cookie (200 expected, the right identity is returned)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{createApiKeyDay18.response.body.$.apiKey}}

### Create an article with the API key, WITHOUT a cookie (201 expected, authorId = the right account)
# @name createArticleDay18
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{createApiKeyDay18.response.body.$.apiKey}}

{
  "title": "Article créé via clé API",
  "content": "Contenu de test pour le module Public API"
}

### Update this same article with the API key (200 expected, PUT is also covered by the key)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay18.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{createApiKeyDay18.response.body.$.apiKey}}

{
  "title": "Article modifié via clé API",
  "content": "Nouveau contenu"
}

### Invalid key (401 expected, never treated as a real userId)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer cleinventeequinexistepas

### No authentication at all, protected route (401 expected, behaviour unchanged)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

