### ==========================================================
### DAY 19: file upload (multer + magic-bytes validation via
### file-type + non-static storage + PUBLIC/PRIVATE access control
### via /api/uploads).
###
### Multipart upload is not practical to script cleanly in
### .http (binary file required), so the reference test is done with curl
### from a terminal:
###
### curl -c cookies.txt -X POST http://localhost:4000/api/auth/register \
###   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
###   -d '{"email":"upload19@test.com","name":"Upload19","password":"12345678"}'
###
### curl -b cookies.txt -X POST http://localhost:4000/api/uploads \
###   -F "file=@monimage.png;type=image/png"
### -> 201 { id, filename, originalName, mimeType, size, visibility: "PRIVATE", ownerId, createdAt }
###
### ==========================================================

### View a PRIVATE upload as its owner (200 expected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/uploads/REMPLACER_PAR_UN_ID_REEL

### Log out
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

### View the same PRIVATE upload, logged out (403 expected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/uploads/REMPLACER_PAR_UN_ID_REEL

### Non-existent upload (404 expected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/uploads/id-inexistant

### Delete an upload without being authenticated (401 expected)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/uploads/REMPLACER_PAR_UN_ID_REEL

### ==========================================================
### DAY 20: profile + avatar (closes the User Management module with
### Day 21). Reuses the Day 19 upload system.
###
### Pitfall to remember if a Prisma field/relation ever "does not exist"
### while the schema is correct and the migration applied:
### "prisma migrate dev" does not always regenerate the client by itself.
### If "Unknown argument" appears on a field that does exist in
### schema.prisma -> docker compose exec backend npx prisma generate
### then restart the backend (tsx watch does not watch node_modules).
### ==========================================================

### Create an account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "day20@example.com",
  "name": "Day20",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### View your own profile (default avatar expected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me

### Update your profile (200 expected)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Day20 Renamed",
  "email": "day20-renamed@example.com"
}

### Create an "intruder" account (replaces the current cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "day20-intruder@example.com",
  "name": "Day20Intruder",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### The intruder tries to take the email already used by the other account (409 expected)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Peu importe",
  "email": "day20-renamed@example.com"
}

### View the PUBLIC profile of another account (no email in the response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/REMPLACER_PAR_UN_ID_REEL

### Non-existent profile (404 expected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/id-inexistant

### Link an upload as avatar (you need to have uploaded a file
### via /api/uploads beforehand, see Day 19 - replace the id below):
### 200 expected, avatarUrl updated, and the upload switches to PUBLIC.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/avatar
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "uploadId": "REMPLACER_PAR_UN_ID_REEL"
}

