### ==========================================================
### DAY 25: optional 2FA (TOTP), enabled from the profile.
### The 6-digit code changes every 30 s and cannot be generated by this file. To get one:
###   1. copy the "secret=..." parameter of the otpauthUrl returned by the setup (or read twoFactorSecret in the database)
###   2. from the project root:
###      docker compose -f platform/docker-compose.yml exec backend node -e "console.log(require('otplib').authenticator.generate('LE_SECRET'))"
###   3. paste the code into the @totpCode variable below (redo it before EACH request that uses it)
### Wrong codes / passwords count against authLimiter (10 failures / 15 min / IP): if 429, `make restart`.
### ==========================================================

@totpCode = 763533

### Create a dedicated account (409 if already created: go straight to login)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "twofa@example.com",
  "name": "twofa",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Profile: twoFactorEnabled = false
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me

### Start the activation: returns otpauthUrl + qrCode (data URL). The secret is stored but 2FA is NOT active yet
# @name twoFaSetup
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/2fa/setup

### Activate with a wrong code (400 expected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/2fa/enable
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "000000"
}

### Activate with a code in the wrong format (400 expected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/2fa/enable
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "abc"
}

### Activate with a valid code (200, twoFactorEnabled: true) — update @totpCode first
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/2fa/enable
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "{{totpCode}}"
}

### Profile: twoFactorEnabled = true
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me

### Run the setup again while 2FA is active (409 expected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/2fa/setup

### Log out
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

### Correct password login: no session, { requires2fa: true } expected
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "twofa@example.com",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Must be 401: the "pending" state opens no access
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### Must also be 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard

### Wrong code (401 expected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login/2fa
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "000000"
}

### Wrong format (400 expected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login/2fa
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": 123456
}

### Right code (200, session opened) — update @totpCode first. If the code was already used within the last 30 s, wait for the next one
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login/2fa
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "{{totpCode}}"
}

### Now logged in (200 expected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### Replay /login/2fa without a prior login: the pending state was consumed (401 expected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login/2fa
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "{{totpCode}}"
}

### Disable with a wrong password (401 expected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/2fa/disable
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "mauvaismotdepasse",
  "code": "{{totpCode}}"
}

### Disable with the right password but a wrong code (400 expected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/2fa/disable
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "motdepasse123",
  "code": "000000"
}

### Disable with both correct (200, twoFactorEnabled: false) — update @totpCode first
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/2fa/disable
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "motdepasse123",
  "code": "{{totpCode}}"
}

### Disable while 2FA is already off (400 expected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/2fa/disable
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "motdepasse123",
  "code": "{{totpCode}}"
}

### Log out then log in again: classic login, without requires2fa
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "twofa@example.com",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Without authentication: setup refused (401 expected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/2fa/setup


### ==========================================================
### ARTICLE DOCUMENT (PDF): the PDF stays PRIVATE in the database at all times,
### access is computed dynamically via canViewArticle,
### same rule as the article's own visibility:
### PUBLISHED -> everyone, otherwise the author or any
### logged-in user if SUBMITTED, otherwise nobody
###
### curl -c cA.txt -X POST http://localhost:4000/api/auth/register \
###   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
###   -d '{"email":"docauthor@example.com","name":"author","password":"motdepasse123"}'
###
### curl -b cA.txt -X POST http://localhost:4000/api/uploads \
###   -F "file=@monfichier.pdf;type=application/pdf"
### -> 201 { id, ... } : this is the DOC_ID
###
### curl -b cA.txt -X POST http://localhost:4000/api/articles \
###   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
###   -d '{"title":"Test doc","content":"contenu","documentId":"DOC_ID"}'
### -> 201 { id, ... } : this is the ART_ID to replace below
###
### ==========================================================

### The author sees documentUrl even in DRAFT (the PDF is theirs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/REMPLACER_PAR_ART_ID

### The author downloads their own document in DRAFT (200 expected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/REMPLACER_PAR_ART_ID/document

### Create a second "third party" account (replaces the current cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "doctiers@example.com",
  "name": "tiers",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### The third party does not see the DRAFT article (404 expected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/REMPLACER_PAR_ART_ID

### The third party cannot download the document of a DRAFT (404 expected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/REMPLACER_PAR_ART_ID/document

### Log in as the author to submit the article
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "docauthor@example.com",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/REMPLACER_PAR_ART_ID/submit

### Log in as the third party (now a potential reviewer since it is SUBMITTED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "doctiers@example.com",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### The third party now sees documentUrl (article SUBMITTED)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/REMPLACER_PAR_ART_ID

### The third party downloads the document while SUBMITTED (200 expected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/REMPLACER_PAR_ART_ID/document

### Log out: check that an anonymous visitor neither sees nor downloads a SUBMITTED article
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

### Anonymous, SUBMITTED article (404 expected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/REMPLACER_PAR_ART_ID

### Anonymous, download of a SUBMITTED document (404 expected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/REMPLACER_PAR_ART_ID/document

### Log in as the third party to review and approve
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "doctiers@example.com",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### @name docReview
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/REMPLACER_PAR_ART_ID/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "comment": "ok"
}

###
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/{{docReview.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "APPROVED"
}

### Log out: the article is PUBLISHED, the PDF must be public
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

### Anonymous downloads the document of a PUBLISHED article (200 expected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/REMPLACER_PAR_ART_ID/document


